Z||000000||FieroJoe||12-11-2000||10:59 AM||||I've seen the different "high output" headlight kits from the Fiero Store for around $70-$80.  They are either Blue, Super White, or Gold.  Anybody have these in their car, and are they worth the extra cash?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||12-11-2000||12:26 PM||||well, i don't have them right now, but planning on getting some. you ask if they're worth it. well, they put out better light (i hope), look better IMO, and when you replace a light, you just have to buy a $2-3 light bulb instead of the whole light assembly for $10-15. i'm pretty sure about this, but don't hold me to it. hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PlasticWrapd||12-11-2000||02:38 PM||||IMHO, the only lights to have are the E-spec H4's.  E-spec lights have superior light patterns and illuminate the road far better than <I><B>ANY</B></I> US-spec light, bar none.  I have a pair of the E-spec lights, complete with parking lights and 80/100 H4 bulbs.  If I ever sell one of my cars, the headlights come out and are replaced with standard halogen sealed beams.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-11-2000||02:55 PM||||the Fiero Store kits are ok.. but you need a set of Hella H-4 conversions.. they are about the same sprice and you'll be MUCH happier with them.. call Chris or Danny at NOPI in smyrna, ga 770-434-0051  you'll need the 6045 to H4 Hella conversion.. THEY ROCK!!! had set in my SE.. have Catz XLDs in my GT.||||reg||1
Z||000004||86_Fastback||12-11-2000||03:06 PM||||I have the the H4 housing and bulbs.  Definatly worth the money for the better lighting.  One place to get good bulbs at a reasonable price is at <A HREF="http://www.AutoOptiks.com." TARGET=_blank>www.AutoOptiks.com.</A>   They also carry the housings I believe for $50.  Of course you need to buy bulbs if you get their housings, but there is a good selection.<BR>I have the Fiero Stores housings on my Fiero, but I have Auto Optiks on my 1998 Pontiac TA (only ones that I know that have these housings and they use H7 bulbs).  The ASTRA DICHROIC ION-GOLD are good for bad weather (lows on my TA) and the ASTRA CLEAR<BR>HIGH OUTPUT are good for clear weather (high beams in my TA).  Their site is pretty informative.<BR>You won't be dissappointed.<P>Gregg<P><BR>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 86_Fastback (edited 12-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-11-2000||07:50 PM||||Thanks alot everyone, I'll have to examine those choices.  My car's already hit one deer (not bad at all, just cracked a tiny bit of the front fascia, left some hair on it), and I live in an area with lots of deer crossings across the roads.  I hunt too (with a gun, not my car)<P>But anyways, thanks again!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||Rodrv6||12-11-2000||09:50 PM||||I've got a set of Cibie Z-Beams in mine.  I really like the pattern on the low beams. It's much better than stock sealed beams.  Changing a burned out bulb is a 3 minute, no tool job!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
